  ('AUD-82A941003', 5, 'Plugged straight in (A5 F5)', 'Cross-referenced the OE number against my 2023 A5 F5 before ordering. Swapping it over took an afternoon working carefully. The internal reflector finish looks the same as the unit that came off. Result is the cut-off is sharp and sits exactly where the old one did. Will be back for the other side.', 'Priya Novotny', true, TRUE, '2026-03-21T23:05:38.208Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 4, 'Primed and ready to paint', 'Ordered this for my A6 C8 after the original gave up at 118k. It clipped into the factory mounting points without drilling anything. The swage lines and body contours follow the original exactly. Result is the paint match came out perfectly with no ripple in the reflection.', 'Lena Bergmann', true, TRUE, '2025-04-23T12:33:13.787Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 3, 'Fits well, arrived slightly marked', 'Ordered this for my A1 8X after the original gave up at 61k. It clipped into the factory mounting points without drilling anything. The swage lines and body contours follow the original exactly. On balance the paint match came out perfectly with no ripple in the reflection. Fine for the money, with that one caveat.', 'Jonas Duarte', false, TRUE, '2025-06-12T11:35:52.827Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 3, 'Good panel, treat the tabs gently', 'Fitted to my 2014 Q5 8R. I prepped and painted it in the car colour and it went on in a morning. One of the mounting tabs sheared as soon as it was put under any tension. That said, the finished repair cost a fraction of a dealer panel. Good part, minor niggles.', 'Elena Rossi', true, TRUE, '2025-10-10T21:55:39.435Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 4, 'Saved a fortune on the repair', 'Ordered this for my Q7 4M after the original gave up at 131k. The steel gauge feels the same as the original panel we cut out. It clipped into the factory mounting points without drilling anything. Result is the panel gaps are even down both sides and you cannot tell it was repaired.', 'Patrick Silva', true, TRUE, '2026-02-17T06:11:51.798Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 4, 'Bodyshop was impressed', 'Second one of these I have bought, this time for the Q7 4L. The steel gauge feels the same as the original panel we cut out. I lined it up against the door shut and the gap fell straight in. Result is the finished repair cost a fraction of a dealer panel. Will be back for the other side.', 'Nadia Castellanos', true, TRUE, '2025-04-19T02:09:40.458Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 3, 'Fits well, arrived slightly marked (Q7 4M)', 'Ordered this for my Q7 4M after the original gave up at 151k. The bodyshop test-fitted it before paint and needed almost no adjustment. It arrived with a crease along one edge because the packaging was inadequate. That said, the paint match came out perfectly with no ripple in the reflection. Good part, minor niggles.', 'Tobias Castellanos', true, TRUE, '2025-08-31T21:29:30.322Z'),
  ('AUD-89A810422A', 4, 'Lined up first time', 'Replacement for my 2020 Q8 4M 2.5 TFSI. I lined it up against the door shut and the gap fell straight in. The steel gauge feels the same as the original panel we cut out. Result is it has been on a year now with no sign of corrosion at the seams. Exactly what I needed.', 'Yara Silva', false, TRUE, '2026-01-18T17:20:53.698Z'),
  ('AUD-8B3133844B', 5, 'Correct fit, sealed properly', 'Ordered this for my S3 8V after the original gave up at 49k. I changed it with the oil at the same service interval. Dimensions matched the outgoing filter to the millimetre. Result is the musty smell from the vents has completely gone. Will be back for the other side.', 'Elena Kaur', true, TRUE, '2025-10-13T18:27:57.888Z'),
  ('AUD-8B3133844B', 4, 'No leaks, no fuss', 'Cross-referenced the OE number against my 2017 A8 D4 before ordering. I pre-oiled the seal before fitting and there has not been a drop since. The media feels dense and the end caps are properly bonded rather than glued on thin. Result is shifts are smoother now the transmission has clean fluid and a fresh filter. Good value against the dealer price.', 'Martin Ellery', true, TRUE, '2026-03-31T03:10:17.637Z'),
  ('AUD-8B3133844B', 5, 'Exactly what the service needed', 'Second one of these I have bought, this time for the S3 8V. Dimensions matched the outgoing filter to the millimetre. I changed it with the oil at the same service interval. Result is no leaks at all after several hundred miles.', 'Thomas Brandt', true, TRUE, '2025-06-19T00:32:31.523Z'),
  ('AUD-8F0839479E', 5, 'Panel gaps came out perfect', 'Replacement for my 2015 Q5 8R 2.5 TFSI. All the mounting tabs and clip locations are present and in the right place. It clipped into the factory mounting points without drilling anything. Result is it has been on a year now with no sign of corrosion at the seams.', 'Thomas Marchetti', true, TRUE, '2025-07-27T01:47:43.075Z'),
  ('AUD-8F0839479E', 4, 'Lined up first time', 'Fitted to my 2019 A5 F5. The bodyshop test-fitted it before paint and needed almost no adjustment. The swage lines and body contours follow the original exactly. Result is the panel gaps are even down both sides and you cannot tell it was repaired.', 'Talia Sorensen', true, TRUE, '2025-10-21T22:02:37.511Z'),
  ('AUD-8F0839479E', 5, 'Bodyshop was impressed', 'Ordered this for my Q5 FY after the original gave up at 100k. All the mounting tabs and clip locations are present and in the right place. I prepped and painted it in the car colour and it went on in a morning. Result is the panel gaps are even down both sides and you cannot tell it was repaired.', 'Adrian Whitfield', true, TRUE, '2026-07-10T23:50:13.229Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 2, 'Thread pitch was wrong', 'Replacement for my 2019 S3 8V 2.0 TDI. The thread pitch did not match my originals and I had to source them elsewhere. They threaded in cleanly by hand before I put a socket anywhere near them. Disappointing for the price.', 'Patrick Delgado', true, TRUE, '2025-04-16T11:15:46.704Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 5, 'Correct thread, correct grade', 'Bought for a 2012 A7 4G. Thread pitch and length are spot on against the old hardware. Torqued to the manual figure with no sign of stretch. Result is no corrosion on them after a winter of road salt.', 'Lena Ibrahim', true, TRUE, '2025-09-03T14:19:03.899Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 3, 'Right bolts, count was short', 'Replacement for my 2010 A5 8T 3.0 TDI V6. I replaced the whole set rather than reuse stretch bolts, as you should. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. On balance no corrosion on them after a winter of road salt. Worth buying, just go in with your eyes open.', 'Rebecca Rahman', true, TRUE, '2025-12-18T07:43:54.227Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 5, 'Proper OE spec', 'Second one of these I have bought, this time for the Q7 4M. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. I replaced the whole set rather than reuse stretch bolts, as you should. Result is everything torqued down evenly with nothing binding.', 'Jonas Novotny', false, TRUE, '2025-09-04T21:51:49.787Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 5, 'Saved a trip to the dealer', 'My RS4 B7 needed this doing at 146k miles. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. Torqued to the manual figure with no sign of stretch. Result is it came in cheaper than the dealer wanted for the same specification.', 'Oscar Novotny', true, TRUE, '2026-07-24T15:43:47.222Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 5, 'Exactly the right hardware', 'Fitted to my 2008 TT 8J. I replaced the whole set rather than reuse stretch bolts, as you should. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. Result is everything torqued down evenly with nothing binding. Delivery was quick too.', 'Rajesh Ferreira', true, TRUE, '2025-08-07T18:00:31.570Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 5, 'Right first time', 'Bought for a 2008 A6 C6. I replaced the whole set rather than reuse stretch bolts, as you should. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. Result is everything torqued down evenly with nothing binding. Delivery was quick too.', 'Hannah Whitfield', true, TRUE, '2025-05-30T02:17:08.659Z'),
  ('AUD-8K0805399A', 3, 'Good hardware, slow to arrive', 'Cross-referenced the OE number against my 2007 A4 B7 before ordering. I replaced the whole set rather than reuse stretch bolts, as you should. Proper grade steel rather than the soft plated stuff that rounds off. On balance everything torqued down evenly with nothing binding. Fine for the money, with that one caveat.', 'Talia Kaur', true, TRUE, '2025-11-07T19:03:43.904Z'),
  ('AUD-8MA512131B', 5, 'Car feels new again', 'Replacement for my 2015 Q3 8U 2.0 TDI. Damping is progressive when you compress it by hand, not dead at the top of the stroke. I torqued everything at ride height rather than with the suspension hanging. Result is the clonk over speed bumps that started this job has completely gone.', 'Emre Ibrahim', false, TRUE, '2026-03-21T06:24:53.520Z'),
  ('AUD-8MA512131B', 5, 'Well damped, not harsh', 'Cross-referenced the OE number against my 2003 A3 8P before ordering. I torqued everything at ride height rather than with the suspension hanging. The rod is properly finished with no machining marks and the seal is clean. Result is the clonk over speed bumps that started this job has completely gone. Happy to recommend it.', 'Malik Halvorsen', true, TRUE, '2026-01-05T10:41:15.181Z'),
  ('AUD-8MA512131B', 3, 'Good dampers, buy the top mounts too', 'Bought for a 2011 Q3 8U. The garage did the pair and the alignment came back within spec straight away. Damping is progressive when you compress it by hand, not dead at the top of the stroke. On balance body roll through roundabouts is properly controlled again. Fine for the money, with that one caveat.', 'Martin Delgado', true, TRUE, '2026-01-19T11:02:13.385Z'),
  ('AUD-8MA512131B', 5, 'Crashing over potholes has stopped', 'Replacement for my 2024 A4 B9 2.5 TFSI. Top mounts and bearings went on at the same time while it was apart. The paint and plating look like they will survive a few winters of salt. Result is the car no longer floats over crests and settles in one movement.', 'Lena Novak', false, TRUE, '2026-06-11T15:52:17.474Z'),
